{
  "$comment": "Fingerprints of every sample in test-output/samples/ (written by the BUILT CLI, scripts/generate-samples.ts). Regenerate deliberately with `npx tsx scripts/verify-samples.ts --update`, and say why in the release notes: a changed hash means existing output changed. Mode `bytes` is a SHA-256 of the file; mode `semantic` is a SHA-256 of a canonical projection of the document, used for encrypted samples (CSPRNG file key and IVs) and signed samples (a per-revision /ID drawn at signing time), whose bytes can never repeat. Each entry's `since` names the release whose output the hash is: it is carried forward untouched while the sample is unchanged, and moves to the release doing the rebaseline when the hash changes, so the chain 1.5.0 -> 1.6.0 -> … stays auditable and every re-anchoring is visible in the diff.",
  "baselineVersion": "1.6.0",
  "provenance": "Initial baseline, captured on the release/v1.5.0 branch with pdfnative 1.8.0 by the built CLI (scripts/generate-samples.ts). No earlier reference exists: pdfnative-cli 1.4.0 had no determinism plumbing (no --creation-date, no SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH, samples rendered by a globally installed binary through a shell). Every render sample was checked byte-identical across two consecutive generator runs and across time zones (TZ=UTC pinned by scripts/helpers/tz.ts, instant pinned by --creation-date + SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH); the 6 encrypted and 4 signed samples are semantic by construction (CSPRNG file key / per-revision signature ID). Later rebaselines: keep this note, append the reason for each re-anchored group, and name it in the release note. v1.6.0 (release/v1.6.0, pdfnative 1.9.0): 36 entries re-anchored and 8 added, one rebaseline. Moved: every sample embedding a font (lean, compact subsets under the six-letter tag; engine ledger C6, C21, C28), every untagged document with shaped or right-to-left text (/Span /ActualText on reordered and right-to-left runs; C20, C27), every shaped run (one text object per line; C25), the watermark samples (page transparency group; C11), the tagged documents (table semantics /Scope, /Headers, /IDTree; C12), annotate/linked.pdf (the /Link body is the engine's since #91), attachments/01-pdfa3-with-xml.pdf (invoice.xml normalised to LF with the repository) and table-variant/01-financial-transactions.pdf (infoItems as { label, value }, the shape the engine types). Added: the five 1.9.0 Indic scripts, --direction auto, spot colours under PDF/X-4, the PDF/A-2b + PDF/X-4 dual claim, a JPEG 2000 image, per-bar chart colours, a 160-entry table of contents, and ltv embed from offline material (semantic, like its signed source; the projection now records the /DSS inventory).",
  "creationDate": "2026-01-01T00:00:00.000Z",
  "timezone": "UTC",
